  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Smalta",
    "overview": "Sarap is laid out like an Almaty modernist mosaic panel: a smalt-ultramarine shell over a concrete ground, with turquoise, ochre and terracotta tesserae set in near-black grout. Everything the engine understood becomes a tile. The query is read back as a sentence of coloured tesserae, each expert's score is a 10×10 field filled one tile per percent, availability is a square tile beside a word, and the brand mark itself is five tiles forming an S.\n\nThe system is flat, square and dense in the way a mosaic is dense: small gaps (1–2 px grout) between solid fields, never soft cards on white. Display type is a wide modernist face set light and tight; UI text is a calm humanist sans. Colour carries meaning, not decoration: turquoise is a confirmed skill or a strong score, ochre is place or the primary action or a medium score, smalt is a condition or the shell, terracotta is what was excluded, grey is weak.\n\nIt refuses the category default of a white SaaS list with a blue pill and a progress bar. A weak result is drawn grey and listed plainly; it never gets the blue panel.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Square everything: zero radius on buttons, inputs, selects, checkboxes, panels, tiles.",
      "Mosaic grammar: solid tiles separated by thin grout gaps (1–2 px), dark 2 px grout rules under section titles.",
      "Meaning by tile colour, always paired with a word or a number.",
      "Light, wide Unbounded numerals at very large sizes; tabular figures for every score and count.",
      "Smalt shell top and best-candidate panel; concrete page; plaster for raised light surfaces; grout footer."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
